Amazon Bedrock AgentCore – Identity & Inbound Authentication Validation
Objective

Validate that AgentCore Runtime supports secure inbound authentication using external Identity Providers (IdPs) via JWT bearer tokens, and confirm that unauthorized or tampered tokens are rejected before agent execution.

The goal of this testing was to confirm that:

AgentCore can validate JWTs issued by an external IdP (Auth0).

Invalid or tampered tokens are rejected immediately.

Valid tokens are accepted and forwarded to the runtime execution layer.

