Tests Performed
Test 1 — Valid JWT Invocation

Steps

Generated an access token from Auth0 via /oauth/token.

Pasted the JWT into the AgentCore Sandbox invocation panel.

Invoked the runtime endpoint.

Result

Agent invocation failed (500)

Interpretation

Authentication succeeded.

Request passed the JWT validation layer.

Invocation reached the agent runtime execution stage.

Failure occurred downstream (likely model invocation / SCP restriction).

This confirms JWT authentication is working and requests are allowed past the gateway when valid tokens are supplied.

Test 2 — Tampered JWT Signature

Steps

Modified a single character within the JWT token.

Attempted invocation again.

Result

Invalid Signature for bearerToken

Interpretation

AgentCore correctly rejected the request during JWT signature validation.

This confirms:

Runtime retrieves IdP JWKS public keys

JWT signature is cryptographically verified

Tampered tokens are rejected immediately
